## Growth Trajectory Tracking

The synthesis loop stores a daily snapshot as a `__system_snapshot__` row in `six_quotient_growth`. This snapshot contains per-quotient quality ratios (positive / total signals) and top anti-patterns. Over weeks, these snapshots create a trajectory that shows whether each quotient is improving, stable, or needs attention.

| Quality Ratio | Trajectory |
|---|---|
| > 0.7 | Improving |
| 0.4 – 0.7 | Stable |
| < 0.4 | Needs attention |

## When Adding a New Anti-Pattern

1. Add the regex to `_QUALITY_ANTIPATTERN` in `six_quotient_growth_engine.py`
2. Add the correction to `_ANTIPATTERN_CORRECTIONS` with a WRONG/RIGHT example
3. Update this rule's anti-pattern table
4. The growth engine will automatically detect, log, and crystallize it

## When Updating Assessment Scores

After a new formal Six-Quotient Assessment:
1. Update `BASELINE_SCORES` and `COMPOSITE_BASELINE` in `six_quotient_growth_engine.py`
2. Update the `six-quotient-assessment-baseline.mdc` rule with the new scores
3. Update the baseline table in this rule
4. Seed updated quotient self-measurement crystals via new migration
